[00:11.71] Did you see our brother?
[00:16.17] He was here the other day
[00:19.73] But he only came to say that he was leaving
[00:27.79] Did you see his lady?
[00:32.04] She was looking where he'd gone
[00:35.62] But she wasn't letting on that she was grieving
[00:44.07] She's bound to go
[00:48.49] Perhaps she'll find him waiting for his boat in some city far away
[00:59.80] She's bound to go
[01:09.31] Lately I remember
[01:13.42] Afternoons of smoke and wine
[01:16.82] There was nothing we could find but peace and pleasure
[01:24.70] And with a smile he told me
[01:29.39] That he wanted just to be
[01:32.76] On his way across the sea no man can measure
[01:41.46] He won't be back
[01:45.74] And the sun may find him sleeping in the dust of some ruin far away
[01:57.21] He won't be back
[02:05.27] Early today as I watched while the skyline was shaking
[02:12.92] I heard a rumbling
[02:17.63] Early today the mechanical city was waking
[02:25.24] And I ran out stumbling, mumbling
[02:30.14] Out through the laughter of children and dogs
[02:40.81] Did you see our brother? (Someone who had been away)
[02:45.15] He was here the other day (Suddenly came back today)
[02:47.78] (And I allowed a hope to stray into my mind)
[02:48.63] But he only came to say that he can't breathe here
[02:56.76] Did you see his lady? (For the moment, face to face)
[03:01.15] She was reaching for his hand (We looked back upon the place)
[03:03.79] (Where long ago we went to chase our careless time)
[03:04.72] Just as if to tell her man that she can't either
[03:13.26] They're bound to go (Oh, what do you know?)
[03:17.47] And the sun may find me running after them (Not what I've been feeling)
[03:21.85] Seeing something far away (The past is healing so slow)
[03:28.96] We won't be back (By tomorrow gone from sorrow)
[03:41.10] 